  "finding": "Conditional architecture NOT demonstrated on dev data. Raw counts help modestly everywhere (raw_only FPR 0.1051 vs norm_only 0.1048 at matched >=99.5% recall); they are not uniquely valuable in under-covered entities (their FN are missed by BOTH models -- 16/19 shared). The raw+rate combination (V_rawplus 0.0992) already captures both signals globally; a per-entity conditional switch is not justified by the evidence.",
  "conclusion": "V_rawplus (raw 48 + 6 exposure rates) is dev-robust: >=99.5% recall on the fixed val floor and on all three pre-2018 forward windows with equal/better FPR. Coverage scaling alone does not fix absent-merchant FPR (0.68-0.79 at every level)."
}